  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than six residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining/living rooms shall be retained in perpetuity. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the cycle parking indicated on drawing 'Proposed Block Plan E001 dated 19 June 2025', and prior to the occupation of this development, cycle parking shall be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\r\ro Provision of a minimum of SIX long stay cycle parking spaces.\r\ro in an accessible location: the access route to the long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m;\r\ro secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\ro fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\ro the front boundary wall and gate shall not exceed 1m in height.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision and availability of adequate cycle parking and safeguard the character and appearance of the area.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the occupiers of adjoining premises; protect the general environment; prevent any obstruction to pedestrian movement and to ensure that there are adequate facilities for the storage and recycling of recoverable materials.\r",
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\r Site Location Plan 27.10.25\r Existing and Proposed Block Plan E001 19.06.25\r Existing Floor Plans E001 09.06.25\r Existing Elevations E002 16.06.25\r Existing Elevations E003 16.06.25\r Existing Section E004 16.06.25\r Proposed Floor Plans P001 20.10.25\r Proposed Elevations P002 20.10.25\r Proposed Side Elevations P003 20.10.25\r Proposed Section P004 20.10.25\r Planning Statement June 2025 \r Flood Risk Assessment October 2025 3860/RE/08-25/01 RevA\r Flood Warning and Evacuation Plan October 2025 3860/RE/08-25/03\r Highway Safety Impact Form\r SuDS Pro Forma Sheet\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r"
  ],
